<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chaldia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chaldia was a mountainous region of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> inland from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a>, around present-day Gümüşhane, named after the ancient Chaldoi. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> it became a military province (theme) in the ninth century, with Trebizond as its capital. In the Empire of Trebizond it was a frontier district held by powerful local families who supplied soldiers but often acted on their own.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chaldia.jpg" alt="Chaldia" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cplakidas · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Asia_Minor_ca_842_AD.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
